  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 310 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nThe front will still be making its way through Sunday, and if it \nmanages to kick off any rain, that may be lingering. The ridge \nwastes no time making up for its minor retrograding and builds east \nagain Sunday. Heat Index values 100-110 are expected once again. \nThough the front will be quite weak, it does sweep away some of the \nhigher dewpoint temperatures to the west, and the western portion of \nthe area may be several degrees cooler for Monday.\n\nBy Tuesday, the low pressure to the northwest begins to break down \nthe ridge and sends a more classic cold front our way. The day 6-7 \nmodel output is showing the potential for up to 35% PoPs into \ncentral Missouri Wednesday night with 20% odds widespread across our \nCWA by Thursday morning. This system will be watched closely in the \ncoming days as it is our best hope for any respite from the \nheat, however short lived.",
